EXAMPLE 5: THE ACRONYM THAT WAS NOT THERE
Source: Q 5 tab
==========================================

ASKED: "What facilities in North America do HCT occupy?"

WRONG: returned a summary of all PSLs and site counts pulled from the Top 5
Occupant columns, then asked the user to clarify what HCT meant - after
producing a large table that did not answer the question.

WHY: two problems. The acronym was not resolved, and occupancy was read from
wide Occupant #1-#5 columns, so a PSL sitting in slot 3 was invisible to a query
checking slot 1.

RIGHT - resolve first, flag the inference, then answer:

  I read "HCT" as Completion Tools - that mapping is inferred, not confirmed,
  so check it before relying on the numbers.

  North America - Sites occupied by Completion Tools
  Filters: Active sites, RE Region / MPL = "North America", all occupant slots

  | Site Name | City | Country | Occupant Slot | Current Month NBV |
  ...

If the acronym is NOT in the glossary, do not guess. List the distinct PSL
values present and ask which one - but never produce a large unrelated table
first.


