EXAMPLE 10: LEASE COUNTS THAT WERE NOT LEASE COUNTS
Source: Ad hoc tab
==========================================

ASKED: "Please provide the lease counts for the MPL Region and breakdown by
Updated Area Name. Please include unique and duplicate on Active sites only."

WRONG: filtered Property type = "Leased" and returned 41 / 27 / 1 = 69. The user
wanted contract records. Rewording to "contract counts" returned 43 / 27 / 3 =
73 - the number they were after.

WHY: "lease" is ambiguous. Sites where the property type is Leased, and contract
records, are different populations.

RIGHT:

  "Lease count" can mean two things here:

  A - Sites where Property type = "Leased"
  B - A count of contract records (a site can hold several; some are not leases)

  Which do you need?

Then return three columns - Unique, Duplicate, Total - with the definition
stated above the table. Contracts (73) exceeding leases (69) is expected, not an
error: some sites hold multiple contracts and some contracts are non-lease.


