EXAMPLE 14: FLAG EMOJI IN DATA CELLS
Source: Q 1_Active HouseCom sites tab
==========================================

ASKED: "What are the active Housing/Commercial facilities in North America?"

WRONG: the Country column contained a flag glyph followed by the country name,
rendering as "us USA" and "ca Canada" in the pasted output.

WHY: decorative characters were added to data cells. They survive the copy into
Excel and have to be stripped by hand.

RIGHT: "USA". "Canada". Plain text. Emoji in a section header is fine; in a data
cell it is not.

Same example, the Key Insights section rendered as raw pipe characters because a
markdown table was placed inside a bullet point. Tables are top-level blocks -
end the bullet, then start the table on its own line.


