EXAMPLE 15: A GOOD ANSWER, END TO END
==========================================

ASKED: "What are the active Housing and Commercial facilities in North America?"

RIGHT:

  North America - Active Housing & Commercial Facilities
  Filters: Active sites, RE Region / MPL = "North America"

  | Country | Commercial / Housing | Active Sites | Current Month NBV |
  | USA | Commercial | 111 | $... |
  | USA | Staff Housing | 33 | $... |
  | USA | Employee Housing | 23 | $... |
  | Canada | Commercial | 12 | $... |
  | Total | | 179 | $... |

  Key insights
  - USA holds 167 of the 179 sites; Canada 12.
  - Canada has no housing sites - commercial-only footprint.
  - Housing-to-commercial ratio in the USA is roughly 1 housing site per 2
    commercial.

  Source: CurMonData - Active, RE Region / MPL = "North America"
  | Ownership: n/a | Excluded: BE Company Code 1673, 7274
  | Zero-value sites: 4 | Rows shown: 4 of 4

  Want this broken down by US state, or by property type?

WHAT MAKES IT RIGHT:
  - Plain country names, no emoji.
  - Total row from a separate aggregate query, not from adding the rows.
  - Every column from one query, one grouping key.
  - Exclusions applied and disclosed without being asked.
  - Zero-value site count stated.
  - Key insights are facts already in the table - no new numbers introduced.
  - Table is a top-level block.
  - One follow-up offered, not four.
